{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyKbqeJryD3X85HPLX4e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've made both changes to `utils.js`. As you asked, I didn't run anything, so this is untested.

**What changed:**
- **`slugify`**: after turning whitespace into dashes, it now collapses any run of dashes into one. For example, `"a - b"` becomes `"a-b"` instead of `"a---b"`.
- **`titleCase(s)`**: new function, added to `module.exports` next to `slugify`. It capitalises the first character of each word, where a word is anything between spaces. I avoided the common `\b\w` regex because it treats apostrophes as word breaks and would turn `"don't"` into `"Don'T"`.

**Things to know:**
